# Google service-account keys (Settings -> Integrations -> Google Sheets
# sync) must never be committed - this repo is public (see tauri.conf.json's
# unauthenticated updater endpoint). The real key only ever reaches the app
# via the GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON GitHub Actions secret at CI build time
# (see src-tauri/build.rs) - it is never read from a file in this tree. These
# patterns are just a safety net in case a downloaded key file is ever
# dropped into the project folder for local testing.
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
credentials.json
google-credentials.json
firestore-debug.log

# 2.113.0: what belongs to a release zip and never to the repository. The zip
# holds 1-CLICK-UPDATE.bat and AKO-ZACAT.txt next to a tiqr-manager folder;
# release.ps1 inside that folder removes itself from the clone before it
# commits. These lines keep any of them from being committed by hand.
/release.ps1
/1-CLICK-UPDATE.bat
/AKO-ZACAT.txt
*.zip
# What Windows leaves in folders by itself.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# 2.117.0: the web screens, built by `npm run build:web` and embedded by
# src-tauri/build.rs.
dist-web
# 2.118.0: TIQR for a phone's browser, built by `npm run build:phone` - the
# Rust built for the browser (src/phone/pkg) and the site itself.
src/phone/pkg
dist-phone
